// bubbler profile: agent
//
// A command-line AI agent with no profile of its own. The sandbox has
// the network and nothing else; add the tool and the work to the
// instance's config:
//
//   home-share ".local/bin/<tool>" mode=ro
//     — the binary, read-only; a symlink is resolved on the host. A tool
//       under /usr needs no share at all.
//   command "/home/bubbler/.local/bin/<tool>"
//
// Create the instance once:
//     bubbler create <instance> --profile agent
// then, for every run, name the project and share it for that run only:
//     cd <project>
//     bubbler run <instance> --share .
//
// Credentials belong in the private home (`~/.config/<tool>` inside is
// the instance's own), not in a share of the host's. Deliberately
// absent: an ssh agent, a keyring, the host's dotfiles, a display; a
// tool that nests a sandbox of its own, or drives a browser, needs
// `userns "allow"`.
network
userns "disable"
